KG42.register("clusters-3d5157310e5888a4dba43482",{"id":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v142-d-CL002","paper":"34-market_versus_price_scheduling","label":"Demand-bid aggregation, ISO clearing, and microgrid share allocation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"Demand-bid aggregation, ISO clearing, and microgrid share allocation","market_meaning":"The DMO receives and aggregates demand bids and submits them to the ISO. When the ISO considers demand bids, it performs system social-welfare clearing. After the DMO obtains the awarded quantity, it disaggregates that quantity locally according to the original bids, forming the allocated quantity of each microgrid.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Bid reception, aggregation, ISO clearing of demand bids, and post-award disaggregation are complementary in process and in use. Assurance of the fixed load retains the normal-operation conditions. The institutional form of the DMO is an institutional option within the chain, and a unified market of an independent DMO is not a necessary condition of the process. The index correspondence between ISO bus demand and the DMO total awarded quantity has not been resolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is the conversion of bid information into microgrid allocated quantities, spanning the functions of reception, aggregation, and two-level clearing. Scheduled exchange after allocation and deviation charges have different decisions and obligations. A separate cluster is established for them, and they share the allocation-output interface. All responsibilities are not merged merely because of the same DMO node.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the demand-bid shape, the aggregated submission, and the fixed-load input to aggregation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Is responsible for segment allocation after the award and for accounting of the microgrid allocated quantities, but the mathematical domain and the cross-layer indices are still not closed."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the ISO system-level clearing branch for the case in which demand bids are considered, and does not equate its objective with the DMO local-disaggregation objective."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"The responsibility for receiving bids forms the entry to aggregation. Establishment of the institution in the same chain, and the independent-DMO option, are retained as institutional background and are not turned into necessary dependencies of aggregation or allocation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e037"],"rationale":"The source explicitly describes receiving bids from microgrids and from optional responsive loads, merging the bids, and submitting them to the ISO as associated responsibilities. This supports the functional linkage between reception and aggregation and does not add a C-graph edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"The aggregated demand bids sent by the DMO are the source of the demand bids received by the ISO. The social-welfare branch remains conditional on the ISO considering demand bids. A mathematical identity from the bid curve to the benefit function has not been established on this basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-D-bt","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-D","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The source explicitly states that the ISO award result enters DMO disaggregation, so D_{bt} at both ends is retained as a quantity interface pending verification. The correspondence between bus b and the DMO service domain is not yet clear. This connection does not treat the two objects as already equal in quantity, and it does not directly rewrite total ISO demand as the awarded quantity of a single DMO."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g01-e037"],"rationale":"The same set of microgrid bids both participates in aggregation and serves as the basis for local disaggregation after the award. This supports reuse of bid information. Bid monotonicity cannot directly replace the segment feasible region or the definition of the objective coefficients."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-df","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e031","v141-b-g01-e032","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E18"],"rationale":"The fixed non-responsive load in the bids enters the aggregation accounting and the award accounting of each microgrid, and the conditions that it cannot be changed under normal operation and must be fully supplied are retained. The parameter objects of the two stages are retained separately."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R005::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g02-E21"],"rationale":"These citations use the same demand-bid functional node. The representative item is used only for display. Individual bids, aggregated bids, and the constraints of each stage do not thereby become the same quantity object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g02-E02"],"rationale":"The DMO in the same model undertakes reception, aggregation, and post-award disaggregation. For node display, one representative may be selected. The original node citations, the edges with different directions, and the conditional institutional options are all retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-df-mt","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-df"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e031","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E18"],"rationale":"The source brings the fixed non-responsive bid load of microgrid m in hour t into the allocation accounting, which supports a same-quantity association. The local roles of the aggregation input and the allocation input, and their constraints, are retained separately, and the parameter objects are not merged."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"unverified_source","description":"All source support in this cluster is candidate eligibility, and the unverified status of B is unchanged. A judgment of process compatibility does not constitute a transcription check or an independent scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g01-e035","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check, item by item, the original-page content and scope of application of the bids, Eqs. (11)-(23), and the institutional conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"c_{mj} in the local objective lacks an explicit definition, symbol, and unit. The segment quantities give only an explicit upper bound, which is not yet sufficient to rule out an award to a negative segment. The decision or accounting roles and the units of the response quantity and the awarded quantity, and the mathematical assurance of full supply of the fixed load, still need to be confirmed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-c","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-DX","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-dr","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PDM","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e033","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g01-e036","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Re-extract the coefficient definitions, quantity domain, units, and variable roles of the same mechanism. Do not supply the definition by borrowing a generic c of the same name or the ISO consumer benefit function, and do not write a lower bound into D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"It is not clear whether ISO bus demand is exactly the total awarded quantity of a single DMO, or how the set of microgrids m is assigned to bus b. The written forms of D, D_{bt}, and P^{DM}_{mt} and PD^M_{mt} still need to be checked. Cross-layer equating of quantities cannot be completed merely from identical symbols.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-D","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-PDM","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-D-bt","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e003","v141-b-g01-e034","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"After the mapping among the bus, DMO, and microgrid index sets and the meaning of each symbol are confirmed, decide whether to establish a same-quantity association. At this stage, retain the candidate interface and all original objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R002 has an aggregation expression for the fixed part, but it does not give a complete aggregation expression for the responsive segments or how that expression maps into the ISO consumer benefit and the demand domain. R004 also does not make explicit the assurance boundary of fixed load on the demand side. What is currently supported is process linkage; complete mathematical linkage is not yet supported.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R004::theta::v141-c-R004-theta-lambda-bt","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-D-bt","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B/C is to verify the original-text definitions relating bid aggregation, the benefit function, and the demand feasible region within the same mechanism. Connections not given by the source continue to be marked as gaps, and no new formula is constructed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R003 does not explicitly carry the assumption, stated by the source, that distribution-line capacity is adequate, or the scope in which load shifting is for the time being not modeled. The transmission constraints in R004 cannot replace these allocation-side premises.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify, and have upstream explicitly bind, the assumptions applicable to distribution disaggregation and the cross-period load-shifting scope that is not included. D does not add distribution power-flow or load-shifting constraints."}]},"rule_refs":["34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R002","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R003","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R004","34-market_versus_price_scheduling::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-234e316a4df6b1c7","COMP-c1310ff0c42d5a65","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-fe5714e5a1d65999"]});
